803
00:39:17,689 --> 00:39:20,230
[SPEAKER_02]: You see, we left Shanghai, they was wearing top coats.

804
00:39:20,310 --> 00:39:26,391
[SPEAKER_02]: Right when they passed the date line, and God, man, you landed down there below the international date line, it was hot.

805
00:39:26,611 --> 00:39:27,431
[SPEAKER_02]: Just like in Texas.

806
00:39:27,451 --> 00:39:29,691
[SPEAKER_02]: They was wearing whites, you know, but they're white.

807
00:39:29,711 --> 00:39:32,832
[SPEAKER_02]: We liked to dive after the first game or two we played, and that heat.

808
00:39:33,607 --> 00:39:37,790
[SPEAKER_02]: Then we made port calls to Hong Kong and back around to Yokohama.

809
00:39:37,870 --> 00:39:43,233
[SPEAKER_02]: And then we took nine days to Honolulu, 10 days to Waukee Beach.

810
00:39:43,253 --> 00:39:45,575
[SPEAKER_02]: And we played teams there, Army and everything else.

811
00:39:45,635 --> 00:39:48,037
[SPEAKER_02]: And then we took the boat and landed in Frisco.

812
00:39:50,458 --> 00:39:58,283
[SPEAKER_02]: Then two years later, in 24, the New York Giants and the White Sox, Comiskey and McGraw, took both teams to Europe.

813
00:39:58,664 --> 00:40:00,285
[SPEAKER_02]: We played in England, Ireland, and France.

814
00:40:00,325 --> 00:40:00,825
[SPEAKER_02]: Same teams.

815
00:40:01,453 --> 00:40:03,353
[SPEAKER_02]: I had the whole team, not a small team.

816
00:40:03,413 --> 00:40:05,294
[SPEAKER_02]: I had the whole team of White Sox Giants.

817
00:40:05,514 --> 00:40:06,414
[SPEAKER_02]: That was another trip.

818
00:40:06,634 --> 00:40:08,174
[SPEAKER_02]: That's another trip two years later.

819
00:40:08,214 --> 00:40:09,894
[SPEAKER_02]: I say I got all this out of the game.

820
00:40:10,135 --> 00:40:10,615
[SPEAKER_02]: That's great.

821
00:40:10,655 --> 00:40:10,955
[SPEAKER_02]: Free.

822
00:40:11,375 --> 00:40:15,635
[SPEAKER_02]: And we had, White Sox had to pick up a few players, but some of the others couldn't go.

823
00:40:15,675 --> 00:40:19,696
[SPEAKER_02]: We got Sammy Rice and Val Pacinic from the Washington team.

824
00:40:20,596 --> 00:40:22,717
[SPEAKER_01]: And we had Dave Van Cross.

825
00:40:23,497 --> 00:40:24,397
[SPEAKER_01]: How were you picked in 22?

826
00:40:24,417 --> 00:40:25,877
[SPEAKER_01]: Any particular reason?

827
00:40:26,417 --> 00:40:27,778
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, no, I guess because we could go.

828
00:40:27,798 --> 00:40:29,758
[SPEAKER_02]: We were single and, you know, could get away.

829
00:40:30,890 --> 00:40:33,491
[SPEAKER_02]: Anybody who was specifically invited?

830
00:40:33,551 --> 00:40:34,611
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, Herbie Hunter.

831
00:40:34,651 --> 00:40:36,192
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know why he come to pick on me.

832
00:40:36,272 --> 00:40:38,233
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, I'll tell you why.

833
00:40:38,273 --> 00:40:40,933
[SPEAKER_02]: Charlie Robertson.

834
00:40:41,013 --> 00:40:42,154
[SPEAKER_02]: I think it was Charlie Robertson.

835
00:40:42,234 --> 00:40:50,477
[SPEAKER_02]: Charlie Robertson and Herbie Hunter, and one other man, made a trip over to Japan a year or so before the kind of coaching clinic.

836
00:40:50,737 --> 00:40:52,097
[SPEAKER_02]: They invited them over there.

837
00:40:52,437 --> 00:40:53,698
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's what got it started.

838
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:57,239
[SPEAKER_02]: See, Hunter got to build up this trip.

839
00:40:57,299 --> 00:41:00,300
[SPEAKER_02]: And I think Robertson recommended us, because he used to be

840
00:41:01,485 --> 00:41:03,326
[SPEAKER_02]: on the White Sox in Charlottesville.

841
00:41:03,346 --> 00:41:04,427
[SPEAKER_02]: I imagine it very much.

842
00:41:04,507 --> 00:41:07,348
[SPEAKER_02]: Anyhow, he approached us about if we wanted to go or not.

843
00:41:07,648 --> 00:41:09,089
[SPEAKER_02]: Who put the word in, I don't know.

844
00:41:10,070 --> 00:41:13,872
[SPEAKER_02]: But Luke and Stevie wasn't married either, so they were all single guys.

845
00:41:13,912 --> 00:41:16,953
[SPEAKER_02]: And it's easier to get those guys to go than you could married guys.

846
00:41:17,453 --> 00:41:18,494
[SPEAKER_02]: But some of them had children.

847
00:41:18,514 --> 00:41:20,095
[SPEAKER_02]: They'd have to pay their own expenses.

848
00:41:21,335 --> 00:41:22,936
[SPEAKER_02]: But hey, we'd gone three months and a half.

849
00:41:22,956 --> 00:41:23,977
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a long time.

850
00:41:25,178 --> 00:41:27,679
[SPEAKER_02]: But over the other, we'd only gone about six weeks.

851
00:41:27,719 --> 00:41:28,639
[SPEAKER_02]: We left Montreal.

852
00:41:31,335 --> 00:41:35,278
[SPEAKER_02]: And landed in Liverpool, and we played in Liverpool and Birmingham.

853
00:41:35,298 --> 00:41:37,499
[SPEAKER_02]: Then went over to Dublin, Ireland and played a game.

854
00:41:37,539 --> 00:41:38,800
[SPEAKER_02]: Then we moved into London.

855
00:41:38,820 --> 00:41:41,162
[SPEAKER_02]: We played before the King and Queen in England.

856
00:41:42,042 --> 00:41:44,924
[SPEAKER_02]: And we was all lined up and introduced to him individually.

857
00:41:46,305 --> 00:41:50,929
[SPEAKER_02]: And the Prince of Wales, the one that married the American woman, he was young then.

858
00:41:50,969 --> 00:41:56,572
[SPEAKER_02]: He came right in behind him, the Duke of York, and introduced us all right to him, both lines.

859
00:41:57,173 --> 00:42:00,115
[SPEAKER_02]: So, and the Queen was up in the stands, waving the flag.

860
00:42:01,143 --> 00:42:03,925
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you play cricket fields?

861
00:42:03,965 --> 00:42:06,326
[SPEAKER_02]: No, it was soccer fields, a short center field.

862
00:42:07,247 --> 00:42:10,128
[SPEAKER_02]: They had a—Houns Lobert, you know who he is?

863
00:42:10,448 --> 00:42:12,350
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, he was McGraw's assistant.

864
00:42:12,390 --> 00:42:16,712
[SPEAKER_02]: He'd go out and lay out the diamonds, or help lay them out for the field, see?

865
00:42:17,572 --> 00:42:19,233
[SPEAKER_02]: And they'd be laid out that way.

866
00:42:19,253 --> 00:42:20,814
[SPEAKER_02]: What did the British think of that?

867
00:42:20,854 --> 00:42:21,975
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I don't know.

868
00:42:23,456 --> 00:42:25,497
[SPEAKER_02]: They gave me a write-up in one of the London papers.

869
00:42:25,657 --> 00:42:26,998
[SPEAKER_02]: One of the guys interviewed me.

870
00:42:27,943 --> 00:42:30,664
[SPEAKER_02]: Then we went over to Paris and played a game in Paris over there.

871
00:42:30,684 --> 00:42:34,585
[SPEAKER_02]: Of course, we'd have gone by there because baseball wasn't nothing in Paris.

872
00:42:34,605 --> 00:42:35,865
[SPEAKER_02]: France, they didn't have nothing.

873
00:42:36,945 --> 00:42:41,446
[SPEAKER_02]: Now we sailed and came back to New York on the Leviathan.

874
00:42:41,826 --> 00:42:45,067
[SPEAKER_02]: And we hit a storm and had to stand by for a day as big as that ship was.

875
00:42:47,308 --> 00:42:48,748
[SPEAKER_02]: A day late getting into New York.

876
00:42:49,270 --> 00:42:53,614
[SPEAKER_02]: So I got more of that out of baseball than other people did.

877
00:42:53,775 --> 00:42:54,635
[SPEAKER_01]: You weren't married then?

878
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:54,896
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

879
00:42:54,916 --> 00:42:56,117
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you get married later on?

880
00:42:56,137 --> 00:42:57,138
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I've never been married.

881
00:42:57,178 --> 00:42:57,578
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, I see.

882
00:42:57,598 --> 00:42:59,500
[SPEAKER_02]: My sister's never been married.

883
00:43:00,602 --> 00:43:06,828
[SPEAKER_02]: So then I've been here so long, you know, I've kind of forgotten pro-baseball because I've been tied up in college so long.

884
00:43:09,327 --> 00:43:11,668
[SPEAKER_01]: You coached from 1940 to 75, then?

885
00:43:11,688 --> 00:43:13,029
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, no, not 75.

886
00:43:13,269 --> 00:43:15,210
[SPEAKER_02]: It was 68.

887
00:43:15,330 --> 00:43:15,930
[SPEAKER_02]: 25 years.

888
00:43:16,390 --> 00:43:17,131
[SPEAKER_02]: 1940.

889
00:43:17,171 --> 00:43:18,491
[SPEAKER_02]: 1940 is when I started here.

890
00:43:18,551 --> 00:43:19,592
[SPEAKER_02]: Mr.

891
00:43:19,612 --> 00:43:22,393
[SPEAKER_02]: Dish got sick, and I asked who he wanted.

892
00:43:22,413 --> 00:43:23,754
[SPEAKER_01]: Your old coach, huh?

893
00:43:23,794 --> 00:43:25,194
[SPEAKER_02]: My old coach, and he got well.

894
00:43:25,294 --> 00:43:28,376
[SPEAKER_02]: And I asked him who he wanted to take his place, and he said me, see?

895
00:43:29,116 --> 00:43:34,138
[SPEAKER_02]: So I took it over, and I stayed until 1967.

896
00:43:34,319 --> 00:43:34,739
[SPEAKER_02]: 25 years.

897
00:43:34,779 --> 00:43:37,500
[SPEAKER_02]: Won 20 championships, and finished second three times.

898
00:43:39,171 --> 00:43:40,432
[SPEAKER_02]: Of these?

899
00:43:40,472 --> 00:43:40,772
[SPEAKER_02]: 25.

900
00:43:41,132 --> 00:43:42,353
[SPEAKER_02]: Which conference?

901
00:43:42,373 --> 00:43:43,253
[SPEAKER_02]: Southwest Conference.

902
00:43:43,573 --> 00:43:44,634
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you get to the World Series?

903
00:43:44,894 --> 00:43:45,594
[SPEAKER_02]: Won it twice.

904
00:43:46,035 --> 00:43:47,175
[SPEAKER_02]: Is that right?

905
00:43:47,756 --> 00:43:48,876
[SPEAKER_02]: In Omaha.

906
00:43:49,016 --> 00:43:51,057
[SPEAKER_02]: 1949 and 50.

907
00:43:51,117 --> 00:43:54,639
[SPEAKER_02]: 1949 in Wichita and 50 in first year in Omaha.

908
00:43:55,340 --> 00:43:57,821
[SPEAKER_02]: And I finished second and third up there.

909
00:43:57,881 --> 00:44:01,583
[SPEAKER_02]: I was up there seven or eight times, but I won it twice in a row, two years in a row.

910
00:44:02,935 --> 00:44:03,295
[SPEAKER_02]: That's great.

911
00:44:03,375 --> 00:44:05,636
[SPEAKER_02]: Did any of your boys make it to the big time?

912
00:44:05,656 --> 00:44:08,678
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, there's one played with Cleveland, Max Alvis.

913
00:44:08,798 --> 00:44:09,659
[SPEAKER_02]: He was one of the boys.

914
00:44:09,679 --> 00:44:11,660
[SPEAKER_02]: He left when he was a sophomore.

915
00:44:12,940 --> 00:44:14,521
[SPEAKER_02]: He never quite... Muriel Wall.

916
00:44:15,342 --> 00:44:18,043
[SPEAKER_02]: He was at the Red Sox for a little while.

917
00:44:18,063 --> 00:44:18,763
[SPEAKER_02]: He's a pitcher.

918
00:44:19,544 --> 00:44:22,765
[SPEAKER_02]: He's triple-A mostly.

919
00:44:23,706 --> 00:44:25,467
[SPEAKER_01]: Tell me about when you're...

920
00:44:26,395 --> 00:44:31,898
[SPEAKER_01]: Going out to the field for a game and a clubhouse meeting, do you have these all the time or before a game?

921
00:44:31,979 --> 00:44:32,699
[SPEAKER_02]: You mean where?

922
00:44:32,779 --> 00:44:33,740
[SPEAKER_02]: College or A&R?

923
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:35,441
[SPEAKER_01]: In the club, yeah, in the big time.

924
00:44:35,481 --> 00:44:40,264
[SPEAKER_02]: We used to only have meetings when we opened the season and playing the club the first time.

925
00:44:41,084 --> 00:44:41,624
[SPEAKER_01]: I see.

926
00:44:41,665 --> 00:44:43,045
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that's a new player.

927
00:44:43,486 --> 00:44:45,107
[SPEAKER_02]: And we have some new pitchers and stuff.

928
00:44:45,287 --> 00:44:51,911
[SPEAKER_02]: And they'd go over the lineup and tell you about who did this or who did that, or if anybody played against one of them in the minors, knew something about them.

929
00:44:52,831 --> 00:44:55,333
[SPEAKER_02]: That's usually the goal of them, see, the first trip around.

930
00:44:56,863 --> 00:45:00,104
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, occasionally I'd call something to go over something or do something.

931
00:45:00,124 --> 00:45:02,345
[SPEAKER_02]: But I don't know.

932
00:45:02,365 --> 00:45:04,126
[SPEAKER_02]: I wouldn't say we had a whole lot of meetings.

933
00:45:04,166 --> 00:45:05,106
[SPEAKER_02]: I'd like to do.

934
00:45:05,206 --> 00:45:06,727
[SPEAKER_02]: So I don't know whether I have a lot now.

935
00:45:07,127 --> 00:45:08,528
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't look like it sometimes.

936
00:45:08,848 --> 00:45:10,128
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I don't.

937
00:45:10,148 --> 00:45:11,389
[SPEAKER_02]: Most of them know how to play.

938
00:45:11,449 --> 00:45:20,613
[SPEAKER_02]: Unless you have certain stuff you want to put over, signs or disciplinary stuff you want to talk over that they've got to cut out or somebody had done it.

939
00:45:20,933 --> 00:45:22,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Was there tough discipline in the White Sox in the 20s?

940
00:45:23,014 --> 00:45:25,395
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I didn't have any discipline.

941
00:45:25,415 --> 00:45:25,535
[SPEAKER_02]: No?

942
00:45:27,432 --> 00:45:30,115
[SPEAKER_01]: What were the rules, though?

943
00:45:30,155 --> 00:45:30,815
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't remember.

944
00:45:30,835 --> 00:45:35,719
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, of course, I guess you had them if you were doing it at midnight, most of them do.

945
00:45:37,281 --> 00:45:44,727
[SPEAKER_02]: I remember Peckinpah, he told you to be in by midnight.

946
00:45:44,767 --> 00:45:49,491
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, I used to play, and I used to go out with these gals and friends.

947
00:45:49,531 --> 00:45:52,514
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, if you're going to do any good, you're going to do it by midnight.

948
00:45:52,534 --> 00:45:54,035
[SPEAKER_02]: If you don't, you might as well come on home.

949
00:46:01,887 --> 00:46:05,288
[SPEAKER_02]: You passed right by the ballpark over there.

950
00:46:05,308 --> 00:46:05,968
[SPEAKER_02]: The university?

951
00:46:06,648 --> 00:46:12,989
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, you wouldn't know it because you're looking, but you know when you came on in to the hospital morning, the big round dome on the left?

952
00:46:13,029 --> 00:46:16,370
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that's our new activity center, see?

953
00:46:16,390 --> 00:46:17,230
[SPEAKER_02]: Basketball.

954
00:46:17,810 --> 00:46:20,311
[SPEAKER_02]: And they had the Lawrence Welk show in there.

955
00:46:20,371 --> 00:46:23,812
[SPEAKER_02]: And they had some, just finished some tennis stuff.

956
00:46:23,852 --> 00:46:26,272
[SPEAKER_02]: These pro tennis came in for the tournament last night.

957
00:46:26,952 --> 00:46:29,733
[SPEAKER_02]: And they had a lot of other big league stuff in there.

958
00:46:31,300 --> 00:46:33,898
[SPEAKER_02]: couldn't get together, but they were going to have Barnard and Bailey in there.

959
00:46:33,918 --> 00:46:34,623
[SPEAKER_02]: That belongs to them.

960
00:46:59,006 --> 00:47:01,908
[SPEAKER_02]: Just past that, on the right, you're a little low there coming.

961
00:47:01,928 --> 00:47:02,769
[SPEAKER_02]: You couldn't see it.

962
00:47:03,109 --> 00:47:08,233
[SPEAKER_02]: Just up there about two or three blocks on the right, over a block, was our new ballpark.

963
00:47:08,253 --> 00:47:12,736
[SPEAKER_02]: We got a $2.5 million college baseball field.

964
00:47:12,776 --> 00:47:20,802
[SPEAKER_02]: Past the turf, seats 5,000 with aluminum chair seats in it, big league long benches.

965
00:47:20,902 --> 00:47:28,468
[SPEAKER_02]: And you go up in your clubhouse, nice clubhouses, umpires' dressing rooms, concrete things with a hood out over it.

966
00:47:29,320 --> 00:47:32,242
[SPEAKER_02]: Lights, $125,000 lights.

967
00:47:33,883 --> 00:47:36,025
[SPEAKER_02]: And the name of the park is Dish Falk Field.

968
00:47:36,285 --> 00:47:36,906
[SPEAKER_02]: Is that right?

969
00:47:37,146 --> 00:47:37,946
[SPEAKER_02]: Isn't that nice?

970
00:47:38,807 --> 00:47:39,487
[SPEAKER_02]: Isn't that nice?

971
00:47:41,509 --> 00:47:43,550
[SPEAKER_02]: We're the best in the United States right now.

972
00:47:44,211 --> 00:47:45,432
[SPEAKER_02]: Nobody's got a park that good.

973
00:47:45,452 --> 00:47:49,394
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a college field, I know.

974
00:47:49,434 --> 00:47:50,175
[SPEAKER_02]: It seats 5,000?

975
00:47:50,735 --> 00:47:51,196
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

976
00:47:51,376 --> 00:47:54,738
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's not counting if you put bleachers down inside and add another.

977
00:47:54,998 --> 00:47:56,820
[SPEAKER_02]: How big a schedule do they play over there?

978
00:47:57,467 --> 00:48:00,128
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, last year he played about 51 games.

979
00:48:00,868 --> 00:48:03,209
[SPEAKER_02]: I was limited to 25 when I was coaching.

980
00:48:03,649 --> 00:48:04,730
[SPEAKER_02]: And then they opened the gate.

981
00:48:05,830 --> 00:48:07,971
[SPEAKER_02]: They opened the gate on fall practice.

982
00:48:08,071 --> 00:48:09,392
[SPEAKER_02]: I couldn't have fall practice.

983
00:48:11,472 --> 00:48:14,633
[SPEAKER_02]: Then they let freshmen play.

984
00:48:14,674 --> 00:48:15,854
[SPEAKER_02]: I never could play freshmen.

985
00:48:18,475 --> 00:48:24,217
[SPEAKER_02]: And then what they did, then it's got two or three more teams in the conference now that wasn't in it when I left.

986
00:48:24,737 --> 00:48:26,518
[SPEAKER_02]: Like Texas Tech out there, love it.

987
00:48:27,451 --> 00:48:30,172
[SPEAKER_02]: And Arkansas was too far away, and now they're at it.

988
00:48:30,332 --> 00:48:33,252
[SPEAKER_02]: And the University of Houston is in the conference house.

989
00:48:33,292 --> 00:48:34,413
[SPEAKER_02]: They weren't at it before.

990
00:48:34,433 --> 00:48:36,333
[SPEAKER_02]: So that adds some more teams.

991
00:48:36,373 --> 00:48:38,314
[SPEAKER_02]: So they got 24 conference games.

992
00:48:39,074 --> 00:48:43,975
[SPEAKER_02]: And then you're allowed so many days other than your conference games.

993
00:48:44,875 --> 00:48:51,657
[SPEAKER_02]: And what this guy does, every time he has somebody in here to spring for a game, he plays a doubleheader.

994
00:48:52,957 --> 00:48:54,838
[SPEAKER_02]: They don't say how many games, just days.

995
00:48:55,318 --> 00:48:56,498
[SPEAKER_02]: So he doubles every day.

996
00:48:57,154 --> 00:48:58,775
[SPEAKER_02]: Are these seven innings, a couple of eight?

997
00:48:58,915 --> 00:49:03,598
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, sometimes, yeah, usually seven and nine.

998
00:49:03,638 --> 00:49:04,859
[SPEAKER_02]: Sometimes they'll play more.

999
00:49:04,899 --> 00:49:11,343
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, if Minnesota comes down here, they'll play two seven-inning games, because they've been in the cold so long they haven't been outside.

1000
00:49:12,143 --> 00:49:13,624
[SPEAKER_02]: And they're not ready to play.

1001
00:49:13,664 --> 00:49:16,326
[SPEAKER_02]: The pitchers haven't pitched outside.

1002
00:49:17,067 --> 00:49:20,028
[SPEAKER_02]: So Dick Siebert brings them down here.

1003
00:49:20,048 --> 00:49:22,190
[SPEAKER_01]: Who is the new coach, or your successor?

1004
00:49:22,450 --> 00:49:23,070
[SPEAKER_02]: Gustafson.

